you'd be wrong. Confusius Sulla was a minor Roman philosopher who lived 
around the time of the Emperor Tiberius. he's not noted for any great 
works, primarily because he was drunk most of the time; he is mentioned 
twice in Suetonius, once for vomiting on some rare scrolls in the city 
archives, and another time for setting down a wine goblet on a copy of 
one of Augustus' decrees, which was enough to get him arrested for 
blasphemy and exiled.


